# ============================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages routing rules.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# The app is a single-page application: every screen is served by the same
# index.html and React decides what to render. A static host has no way to know
# that, so a request for a path it does not have on disk returns its own 404.
#
# Without this file, navigating to a sub-path and pressing refresh shows a
# Cloudflare 404 instead of the app - which looks like the site is broken even
# though only the deep link is.
#
# The 200 status is deliberate: it serves index.html WITHOUT redirecting, so the
# URL in the address bar is preserved for React to read. A 301 to "/" would wipe
# the path before the app could route on it.
# ============================================================================

/*  /index.html  200
